ge 3 and the intelliflo planning documents (P1, P4) record Kim's State Pension Age as 66 — a one-year inconsistency within the report and between the report and the cashflow tool inputs.","The Fact Find State Pension Entitlement section (P5) is entirely blank — no figures for Basic State Pension, Additional State Pension, Pension Credit or BR19 projection are recorded for either client.","The report records StatePension as an income category but no gross amounts or start dates are present in the extracted model (confirmed NotPresentInDocument), so the quantum of State Pension income relied upon for affordability is unverifiable from the report alone.","The Fact Find (P6) records a State Pension of only £230 net per month (£2,760 p.a.) for one client, which is materially below the full new State Pension (approximately £11,500 p.a. at the relevant date), yet no explanation or forecast is provided to reconcile this figure.","The intelliflo baseline income statement (P8) shows JS total regular income of £28,613 but only £16,640 employment income is itemised, leaving approximately £11,973 attributable to State Pension/other income — consistent with the cashflow tool figure — but no supporting State Pension forecast document is on file to corroborate this.","No BR19 or State Pension forecast document is present in the evidence pack for either client, leaving the State Pension income figures relied upon in the cashflow modelling unsupported by independent evidence."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The check can be performed to the extent that the available evidence permits, but it reveals several concerns. First, there is a direct internal inconsistency in the report between Kim's State Pension age stated as 66 on page 3 and the cashflow assumption of age 67 on page 14; the intelliflo planning documents (P1, P4) corroborate age 66, making the cashflow input the outlier. This is a data inconsistency within the suitability report itself and affects