ion transfer, consistent with [P7], and is arithmetic-consistent with 3% of the three switching plan values (£110,185). The discrepancy between the report's £1,700 expenditure figure and the Fact Find £1,718 is a data quality issue; the more significant concern is the contradiction between the 'comfortably meets' assertion and the evidenced £288/month deficit, which is a data inconsistency constituting a Potential Concern at Moderate severity.","citations":[{"passageId":"P1","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Total Net Monthly Income","£ 1,430.00"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Total Monthly Expenditure","£ 1,718.00"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Total Monthly Disposable Income","£ -288.00"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Calculated Total Monthly Household Expenditure","£ 1,718.00"]},{"passageId":"P5","source":"intelliflo planning proposed scenario.md","category":"F","quote":"Savings\n## £6,000\nLIQUIDATED 2ND","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"intelliflo planning proposed scenario.md","category":"F","quote":"Kims Income £13,200 p/a (£1,100 Monthly) salary income until 2026 \"Retire (Kim)\" (inflated by 2% p/a)","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"intelliflo planning Baseline scenario.md","category":"F","quote":"Employed, CDH Recruitment £15,600 p/a (£300 Weekly) salary income until 2027 \"Retire (John)\" (inflated by 2% p/ a)","cells":null},{"passageId":"P7","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"we charge an initial advice fee of 3% of the amount invested as per the terms stated in our Client Agreement. In monetary terms this is £3,305.55 with current transfer values, this figure may fluctuate depending on transfer values. This will be paid directly by the pension schemes on transfer.","cells":null},{"passageId":"