uire specific consideration here beyond what CHK-010 addresses.\n\nThe guard noting that 'a ranked comparison placing the recommendation below the existing arrangement is the finding' applies here: the switch report shows the new solution below the existing pension at every growth rate for the overall comparison (P5), and this is material to whether the alternatives rationale is adequately reasoned. The report does not address this in the alternatives section.\n\nThe discrepancy in Kim's State Pension age (66 vs 67) and the inconsistent total fund values (£106,000 / £110,000 / £116,998) affect the factual foundation of the alternatives assessment but are primarily data quality issues rather than alternatives-rationale failures on their own.\n\nOverall: the alternatives section has genuine content and client-specific reasons for most recommendations, but the EA5 cost rationale is directly contradicted by the research, the platform selection lacks documented comparative justification, and the overall projected value reduction from consolidation is not addressed in the alternatives narrative. These are material concerns.","citations":[{"passageId":"P18","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"I do not recommend that you consolidate into this plan as the funds do not meet your risk profile, and the plan itself is 0.06% more expensive than the recommended solution. Plus, they have a £4.50 annual admin charge.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P18","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"the solution is more cost effective than a typical stakeholder pension. Stakeholder pensions also typically do not allow for flexible access and have limited fund ranges.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Mid growth rate – (2.95%)", "Projected value at age 75", "Existing pension: £127,000", "New solution: £115,000"]},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Pension switch repor