ents.","The policy research parateplan notes [P13] show the objective field for each existing arrangement recommendation is blank ('Which objective/goal is this achieving?' — left empty for Aviva, Zurich, People's Pension), indicating the link between each switch recommendation and a named client objective was not completed in the supporting file, and the suitability report does not fill this gap with named objective references for the switch rationale.","The report's mid growth rate for the critical yield is stated as 2.94% in the page 11 narrative but 2.95% in the page 18 appendix (internal inconsistency already noted in extraction).","The combined pension fund value is stated as approximately £110,000 (page 3), approximately £106,000 (page 4), and the individual plan values sum to £116,998.47 per derived figures (or £117,998.47 per extraction note — the derived figures here show £116,998.47), while the recommended solution table shows £110,185 transfer value — none of these agree, and the rationale for consolidation does not acknowledge or reconcile the discrepancy."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The report provides a structured provider and investment rationale, and research documents do exist. However, several consistency concerns arise.\n\n1. Provider selection rationale is wholly generic. Every item under /solution/providerSelection/rationale is flagged isClientSpecific: false. The report makes absolute claims (financial strength, competitive charges, online convenience) without linking them to C1's objectives, circumstances or the comparison platforms. The Defaqto platform research [P1] shortlisted four products but applied no filters and no DNA analysis, so there is no documented feature or charge comparison to corroborate the 'competitive charges' assertion. This is a weak justification finding — absolute marketing claims without comparative evidence, exactly what the guard flags as insufficient.\n\n2. SIPP product selection research [P5/P9] shows one product matched from 118 after filters, with no additional justification text entered. The filters that drove the result are visible in the research file but no qualitative rationale was recorded, leaving the selection supported only by the filter outcome.\n\n3. Investment fund rationale is better evidenced. Fund charges [P10], performance data [P12] and the CIP governance claim [P4] are all consistent with what the research file shows. The active/passive blend, diversification and risk-alignment claims are corroborated by the fund data. The client-specific simplicity preference and risk profile alignment are at least internally stated, though they rest on the report alone (category I passages).\n\n4. The per-arrangement switch rationale in the policy research parateplan [P13] leaves the objective fields blank for all arrangements. The suitability report does provide switch rationale text (lifestyle fund, no adviser servicing, cost) for each switching plan, but the supporting parateplan does not cross-reference named objectives, weakening the evidence that the recommendation was assessed against C1's stated goals.\n\n5. The fund performance claim ('performed well in comparison with their peers') is corroborated by the research performance tables [P12], which show positive discrete and cumulative returns for both funds. This claim stands.\n\n6. The CIP vs investment pathways comparison [P2] and CIP vs single multi-asset fund comparison appear only in category I passages and cannot self-corroborate, but the research file does contain fund-level data consistent with the CIP approach.\n\n7. The vulnerability overlay: the extraction notes /vulnerability/C1/assessment as NotPresentInDocument. No vulnerability characteristics are recorded in the canonical model, so no overlay adjustment is required for this check.\n\n8. The guard on firm panel/CIP membership as legitimate justification applies: the report states the funds are part of the CIP reviewed quarterly, which is a documented process justification. This partially offsets the lack of fresh whole-of-market fund comparison.\n\nOverall: the provider selection rationale is generic and the platform comparison is undocumented beyond a no-filter shortlist, which is a Potential Concern at Low-to-Moderate severity. The investment rationale is better supported but still partly generic. The objective-linkage gap in the parateplan is a secondary concern. This does not rise to High severity because research documents do exist and investment rationale has meaningful corroboration; the primary gap is the absence of a documented comparative platform justification.","citations":[{"passageId":"P1","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["No filters were applied","No filters were applied","No filters were applied"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva Platform","Aviva","No DNA applied"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Elevate","Aberdeen","No DNA applied"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aegon Retirement Choices (ARC)","Aegon","No DNA applied"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Wealthtime Platform","Wealthtime","No DNA applied"]},{"passageId":"P5","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":"No additional justification text has been entered","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Pension Portfolio - Choice","Aviva Life & Pensions UK Limited","No DNA applied"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["HSBC Global Strategy Balanced Portfolio Accumulation C","-","£99.17  (0.18%)","£2.75  (0.01%)","-","£101.92  (0.19%)"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["CT Universal MAP Balanced Fund C Acc","-","£159.77  (0.29%)","£145.05  (0.26%)","-","£304.82  (0.55%)"]},{"passageId":"P12","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["CT Universal MAP Balanced Fund C Acc (GBP)","4.89","9.55","11.17","36.66","44.73",""]},{"passageId":"P12","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["HSBC Global Strategy Balanced Portfolio Accumulation C (GBP)","6.15","9.87","9.92","32.52","40.06","122.95"]},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Test Case 1 - Policy Research -2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva","Switch","","Lifestyle, expensive, no adviser servicing"]},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Test Case 1 - Policy Research -2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Zurich","Switch","","Expensive, no adviser servicing"]},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Test Case 1 - Policy Research -2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["People's Pension","Retain","","Active workplace pension"]},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"The funds are part of our CIP (Centralised Investment Proposition). This is regularly reviewed by a quarterly investment committee. We also utilise a leading external research team to ensure regular monitoring and oversight of our recommended funds.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P17","source":"Zurich Policy Info.md","category":"E","quote":"Guarantees, bonuses, guaranteed minimum pension, safeguarding, life styling, block/bulk transfers, market value reduction, protected or enhanced tax free cash do not apply to this plan.","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Weak justification","Missing evidence"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

