g a fair cost/disadvantage disclosure for that switch. These are Disclosure shortfall and Data inconsistency concerns of moderate-to-high severity.","citations":[{"passageId":"P6","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"The plan itself is 0.08% more expensive than the recommended solution","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Standard Life","0.18%","£186.19","+0.26%","+£268.94"]},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Initial adviser charge of £3,305 which is taken from the new solution, reducing the initial investment accordingly.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P15","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":"This results in a shortfall in the death benefit immediately after the switch of £3,305.00","cells":null},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Effect of switching","–","£10,400 or 9.6% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Effect of switching","–","£12,000 or 9.4% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Effect of switching","–","£15,000 or 10.0% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Mid growth rate - (2.95%)","",""]},{"passageId":"P2","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Based on a mid-growth rate of 2.94%, including our advice fees, the recommended plan would need to grow by 4.8% per year up to age 75 in order to meet the same value as your current plan.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"A switch between pension providers does not guarantee a greater pension fund at retirement and there is no guarantee that the new provider's f